ackDeepFrame` failed at compile: `'apply' redeclared in this block` because the script declared `apply` while `s.Add(\"apply\", ...)` also registers it; the in-script equivalent passed (out=110). The Go-callback variant needs a corrected scratch (script must not redeclare `apply`) and re-run.\n\n[...]\n- require.Equal cannot compare cyclic maps (infinite recursion); use pointer equality.\n- Known pre-existing panic at vm.go:444 (stack slot overwrite before ErrStackOverflow checks) on both branches.\n\n[...]\n11. callable_test.go — appended module/clone/isolation/literal/cyclic tests; check `gofmt -w callable_test.go && go test -run 'TestCallable' ./ 2>&1 | tail -10` — done, all passing.\n12. Temporary scratch_test.go / debug_internal_test.go — diagnostic runs (block globals, stack overflow, formats, many globals, selglobal, cyclic, callback, clones); each removed via `rm -f` after use — Go-callback deep-frame scratch is UNFINISHED (redeclared 'apply'); in-script deep-frame passed (110).\nFinal verification suite: `gofmt -l callable.go callable_test.go compiler.go objects.go script.go vm.go` (clean), `go vet ./...` (clean), `go test -race ./...` (clean), `git diff master --name-only` (compiler.go objects.go script.go vm.go)."}
{"id": "s010", "excerpt": "[...]\n- Works anywhere `cookies=` is accepted (including `Client`/`AsyncClient`/`Request`), keeping existing cookie behavior unchanged otherwise.\n- Supports optional limits `max_cookies` / `max_cookies_per_domain` (ints or None; non-ints → TypeError; negatives → ValueError), evicting deterministically by oldest creation order (per-domain limit enforced first, then global).\n- Parses `Set-Cookie` including multiple cookies combined into one header value (with `Expires=` containing a comma), ignores empty/malformed strings and cookies where `Domain`/`Max-Age`/`Expires` appear without a value, ignores unknown attributes, allows empty values.\n- Implements host-only cookies (no `Domain`), case-insensitive domain matching sent to subdomains, default path derivation, path matching (\"/sub\" matches \"/sub\" and \"/sub/x\" not \"/submarine\"), `Secure` only over https, `__Secure-`/`__Host-` prefix rules, `Max-Age` precedence over `Expires`, deletion on `Max-Age<=0`/past `Expires`, replaced cookies treated as newly created.\n- Sends cookies ordered by longer path first then older creation; `store[\"name\"]` raises `httpx.CookieConflict` on ambiguity.\n- Provides mutable mapping API plus `extract_cookies(response)`, `set_cookie_header(request)`, `set(name, value, domain=\"\", path=\"/\")`, `get(name, default=None, domain=None, path=None)`, `delete(...)`, `clear(...)`, `update(cookies)` accepting `CookieStore`/`httpx.Cookies`/`CookieJar`/`dict`/`list[tuple]`; `set(domain=\"\")`/mapping/list inputs are non-host-only wildcard cookies.\n- Work on new branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master, commit, push to origin, then finish with `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`.\n\n[...]\n### Done\n- Explored repo (`/app`, httpx 0.28.1, master at `b5addb6`). Remote `origin` = `/srv/git/httpx.git` (local bare repo). Remote branch `origin/feature/deterministic-cookie-store` exists at `ea812d9` containing only scratch notes (`scratch/cookie-jar-notes.md`, \"Rough notes, try 2.\").\n- Created local branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master.\n- Created `httpx/_cookie_store.py` (~full implementation): `CookieStore(MutableMapping)`, internal `_Cookie` with `created` counter, `_validate_limit`, quote-aware `_split_set_cookie_header`, `_default_path`, `_domain_matches`, `_path_matches`, `_parse_max_age`, `_parse_expires`, `_parse_set_cookie`, `_store`/`_remove`/`_enforce_limits`, `_matching_cookies`, plus `extract_cookies`, `set_cookie_header`, `set`, `get`, `delete`, `clear`, `update`, `__setitem__/__getitem__/__delitem__/__len__/__iter__/__bool__/__repr__`.\n- Integrated: `httpx/__init__.py` (imports `_cookie_store`, `\"CookieStore\"` in `__all__`), `httpx/_client.py` (`_cookies: Cookies | CookieStore`, isinstance handling in `__init__`, `cookies` property/setter, `_merge_cookies`, `_build_redirect_request`), `httpx/_models.py` (`Request.__init__` dispatches CookieStore; `Cookies.__init__`/`update` converts CookieStore's internal cookies to stdlib `Cookie` objects), `httpx/_types.py` (`CookieTypes` includes `\"CookieStore\"`).\n[...]\n### In Progress\n- Final wrap-up: run final verification/tests, commit on `feature/deterministic-cookie-store`, push to origin.\n\n### Blocked\n- Network is unavailable (only local git remote works); could not fetch upstream httpx 0.29.0 for reference or search GitHub.\n- Remote branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` at `ea812d9` diverges from local branch (created from master) — push will likely need `git push --force origin feature/deterministic-cookie-store` (or accept overwrite of scratch-only branch).\n\n[...]\n- **`set(domain=\"\")` → `host_only=False, domain=\"\"`**: wildcard cookie sent to any host matching path/scheme (mirrors stdlib `domain_specified=False` behavior verified via probes).\n- **Limits enforced on every `_store`** (per-domain eviction of oldest for that domain, then global oldest) — verified invariant holds after each insertion.\n- **Client stores the `CookieStore` instance directly when passed** (`client.cookies is store`), so extraction updates the user's store; `_merge_cookies` merges into a new `CookieStore`.\n[...]\n2. `git add` the changes (`httpx/_cookie_store.py`, `httpx/__init__.py`, `httpx/_client.py`, `httpx/_models.py`, `httpx/_types.py`) and commit on `feature/deterministic-cookie-store`.\n3. Push to origin — likely `git push --force origin feature/deterministic-cookie-store` since the remote branch (`ea812d9`, scratch notes only) has diverging history.\n4. Issue exactly: `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` (no other commands combined).\n[...]\n## Critical Context\n- Working dir: `/app`; Python 3.12.12; remote origin is local bare repo `/srv/git/httpx.git`.\n- Modified files: `httpx/__init__.py`, `httpx/_client.py`, `httpx/_models.py`, `httpx/_types.py`; new untracked file: `httpx/_cookie_store.py`.\n[...]\n- Key internal storage: `self._cookies: dict[tuple[str, str, str], _Cookie]` keyed by `(name, domain, path)`; `_creation` counter via `_next_creation()`.\n- Send ordering: `sorted(..., key=lambda c: (-len(c.path), c.created))`; header built as `\"; \".join(f\"{name}={value}\")`, overwriting existing `Cookie` header.\n- `_default_path`: `path[:path.rfind(\"/\")]` if rfind > 0 else `/`.\n- Only known failing test: `tests/test_timeouts.py::test_write_timeout[trio]` (unrelated, trio unraisable exception; present with network-deselected run `-k \"not test_redirect_loop and not network\"`).\n- Verification script `/tmp/verify_cookie_store.py` covers limits validation, combined headers, host-only/domain matching, default/invalid paths, path matching, secure, prefixes, expiry precedence, replacement ordering, eviction, conflict, wildcard set/dict/list, all update forms, client/async integration, Request `cookies=`, mapping API — all PASS.\n- Remote branch history: `ea812d9 more notes, not working yet` → `ef3b2a7 try a different cookie store approach` → `b5addb6 master`.\n\n[..