/arrays/maps/module exports/Go callback args; variadic; recursion; error message parity; `Clone()` isolation; `Set()` transfer isolation (snapshot captures at transfer, globals resolve to destination); recursive isolation inside transferred arrays/maps.\n2. Run full suite: `go test ./...` (Makefile has `go test -race -cover ./...`); fix any failures (watch `vm_test.go` duplicate-compiled-functions constant dedup test ~line 2765 and error-message tests).\n3. Remove temporary repro files if not converted to real tests.\n4. Commit on `feature/callable-instance-isolation` and push to origin (`/srv/git/tengo.git`; reflog confirms prior pushes work).\n5. Finish with `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`.\n[...]\n- Files modified: `/app/objects.go`, `/app/vm.go`, `/app/script.go`. Temp: `/app/repro_test.go`, `/app/mod_test.go`.\n- Key types: `CompiledFunction{Instructions, NumLocals, NumParameters, VarArgs, SourceMap, Free []*ObjectPtr, ctx}`; `ObjectPtr{Value *Object}`; `frame{fn, freeVars, ip, basePointer}`; `Compiled{globalIndexes, bytecode, globals, maxAllocs, lock}`.\n- VM opcode flow: `OpClosure` (vm.go ~line 747) builds closures with free vars; `OpCall` (~line 636) invokes `value.Call(args...)`; `OpReturn` decrements framesIndex; `OpSuspend` returns from `run()`.\n- Error format reference: `Runtime Error: not callable: int\\n\\tat mod1:3:4\\n\\tat test:4:1` (vm_test.go ~2743); test helper `expectError`/`expectRun` in vm_test.go; `parse()` helper uses file name \"test\".\n- `require.Equal` compares `*tengo.CompiledFunction` via `FormatInstructions` only (require/require.go ~298).\n- Go 1.25.5; tests use package `tengo_test` with `github.com/d5/tengo/v2/require`.\n[...]\n\n## Original Request\nThe user's only message in this segment: \"No questions from my side yet. Keep going.\" — this is a continuation of prior work (earlier context not shown). From the assistant's actions, the task-in-progress is: make tengo's `CompiledFunction` callable directly from Go code (via `Call`), and fix the closure/capture semantics around it — correct behavior for globals, imports, closure captures, recursion, variadics, `Compiled.Clone`, `Compiled.Set`/`Script.Add` transfer between instances, callbacks passed to Go functions, and matching error formatting.\n[...]\n## Progress So Far\n- Verified baseline: full `go test ./...` passed after removing scratch `repro_test.go`/`mod_test.go`.\n- Refactored `callCtx` (objects.go): fields `code` (origin bytecode: constants/source map/file set), `globals` (destination storage), `maxAllocs`, `globalNames` (origin layout), `destNames` (destination layout), `globalMap` (origin→dest index remap), `runtime *runtimeID`. Transferred callables keep origin code/constants but resolve globals against the **destination** instance, remapped **by variable name**.\n- Added `runtimeID` type (with `_ byte` field — zero-size structs shared addresses and broke identity), `sameRuntime(a, b *callCtx)`, `remapGlobals(originNames, destNames)` (nil if layouts identical/unknown), `makeGlobalNames` (script.go), and `SymbolTable.GlobalNames()` (symbol_table.go) tracking **block-scoped** globals by index via `defineGlobalName`/`maxGlobal`.\n- Replaced traversal helpers with cycle-safe, identity-preserving versions sharing a `callableState{cells, funcs, containers}`: `bindContext(ctx, state, snapshot)` on `CompiledFunction` (early return when `sameRuntime`; memoizes funcs; shared `seen` for cells), `resolveObject` (live binding — shares capture cells), `isolateObject` (snapshot — deep-copies captures at transfer time), `containsCallable`/`boundTo` (cycle-safe with seen maps).\n- VM changes (vm.go): `frame` gained `code`, `globalMap`, `layoutNames`; VM gained `ctx`, `globalMap`, `layoutNames`, `runtime`, `retVal`; `newVM(bytecode, globals, maxAllocs, globalNames, runtime)`; `mapGlobal(idx)` returns -1 for undefined names; `OpGetGlobal` yields `UndefinedValue` for unmapped/unknown; `OpSetGlobal`/`OpSetSelGlobal` skip when unmapped