ective for in-progress work on the tengo Go library (`/app`). The work underway (visible from the assistant's actions) is implementing Go-side invocation of Tengo compiled functions: allowing `CompiledFunction.Call(...)` from Go, with correct runtime binding (globals/constants/file set), isolation semantics for `Compiled.Clone()` and callable transfer across instances, and comprehensive tests.\n[...]\n- **script.go**: `Compiled` gains `rt` field; `Compile` creates runtime and transfers globals added via `Script.Add` through a shared memo (preserves aliasing); `Run`/`RunContext`/`Clone` use `c.vm()` / new runtime; `Clone` deep-copies with `snapshotObject` + memo for instance isolation; `Set` transfers/rebinds values into the instance runtime.\n- **callable_issue_test.go** (new, untracked): ~35 tests covering Go-side calls (global functions, closures capturing globals/locals, nested arrays/maps, variadics incl. zero rest, recursion, module exports/imports, bytecode decode round-trip, wrong-arg counts, runtime errors with trace formatting), transfers (snapshot + destination-global resolution, nested shared callables, immutable containers, callback-argument transfer, destination-global mutation only), clone isolation (source/clone, clone-to-clone, containers), `RunContext`, `copy()` callables. Many iterations fixed test expectations and made tests deterministic (Script.Add map iteration order caused flakiness — replaced with Clone/matching global layouts).\n- **Validation**: `go build`, `go vet`, `go test -count=5` repeated runs, and `go test -race ./...` all pass; earlier failures (`.Int()` vs `.Int64()`, nil memo map, divide-by-zero panic, wrong global-index layouts in tests) all resolved.\n[...]\n- All actions were local file edits in the `/app` working tree (via python heredoc scripts + `gofmt -w`): modified `objects.go`, `vm.go`, `script.go`; created `callable.go` and `callable_issue_test.go`. No commits were made.\n- No pushes, force-pushes, branch deletions, rebases, or history rewrites occurred in this session.\n- Authorization: the user's sole message (\"Keep going\") authorizes continuing the implementation work; no separate authorization was given or needed for any git-level operations, and none were performed."}
