tion` values fully callable from Go via `Call`, with correct isolation semantics when callable values cross `Compiled` instance boundaries (`Compiled.Set`, `Script.Add`, `NewScript().Compile()/Run()`, `Compiled.Clone`), matching in-script behavior (globals, imports, closures, variadics, recursion, runtime-error formatting).\n[...]\n### Files created/changed in order (with verification)\n1. **`/app/callable.go`** (new file; patched iteratively, then fully rewritten) — core runtime model: `callableRuntime`, `newRuntime`, `owns`, `contextFor`, `bindLocal`, `isolate`, `newVM`, `call`, `hasForeignCallable(Rec)`, `callableCloner` (maps for fns/ptrs/arrs/iarrs/maps/imaps plus cycle-safe `errs` for `*Error`), `acquireForRuntime`, `acquireArgs`, `bindTouchedGlobals`, `withRuntime`, `buildSlotMap`. Dead code removed along the way (`bindForUse`, `bindCallable`, `cloneCallableValue`, `cloneValue`, `containsCallable`, old `bind`/`isolateFunction` variants). Verified with `gofmt -w`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test -race ./...` after each round. **Finished (all green).**\n2. **`/app/script.go`** — `newRuntime(compiled, …, globalIndexes, …)` for `Compile` and `Clone`; shared cloner isolating foreign callables in globals at Compile; `Set` uses `acquireForRuntime`. Verified by build/tests. **Finished.**\n3. **`/app/vm.go`** — added `frame.runtime`, VM fields `runtime/functionCall/retVal/touchedGlobals`, `frameRuntime()`, `translateGlobal()`, `touchGlobal()`, `runFunction()` (direct Go-side call), `wrapRunError()`, `filePos()`, updated `runtimeError()`, context-aware OpConstant/OpClosure, rewritten OpCall (callee binding + `acquireArgs` for Go callables + per-frame runtime), guards on global opcodes, OpReturn direct-call exit, NewVM own runtime. Suffered two accidents: a botched OpCall rewrite deleted opcode blocks (\"unknown opcode: 21/27\" regressions in `TestScript_SourceModules`) → fixed by `git show master:vm.go > vm.go` then reapplying all patches via python; a `filePos`/frame-`ip` bug broke `TestCall`/`TestVMErrorInfo` etc. → fixed by passing explicit `ip`. Verified with `gofmt`, `go build`, `go test ./...`, `go test -race ./...`, targeted `go test -run 'TestCall|TestVMErrorInfo' -v .`. **Finished.**\n4. **`/app/objects.go`** — `runtime` field + `Call` method on `CompiledFunction` (shown as 28 insertions in `git diff --stat`). Verified via build/tests. **Finished.**\n[...]\n18. **`/tmp/repro/custom_test.go`** (TestCustomObjectClone), **`vmapi_test.go`** (TestDirectVMExposedFunction via parser/compiler/NewVM) — verified custom-object deep copy in Clone and direct-VM callability. **Pass.**\n19. Debug scratch (removed): `/tmp/repro/dbg2_test.go`, `dbg3_test.go`, `min_mod_test.go`, `enum_test.go`, `/tmp/dbg_main.go`, `/tmp/dbg_err.go`, `/tmp/vm.go.bak`.\n\n[...]\n- Repo: `/app`, tengo v2, branch `feature/callable-instance-isolation` over `3cad0da`; uncommitted changes to `objects.go`, `script.go`, `vm.go` + untracked new `callable.go` and `callable_test.go`; docs change in `docs/interoperability.md`.\n- Scratch behavioral suite lives in `/tmp/repro` (module `repro`) with ~37 passing tests; it depends on the local `/app` copy (it compiled against the modified package earlier).\n- Current state at the end of these messages: `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`, `go test -race ./...`, `go vet ./...` all clean; both `/app` and `/tmp/repro` suites pass except intentionally-removed/adjusted tests."}
{"id": "s016", "excerpt": "[...]\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Work on new branch `feature/callable-instance-isolation` from `master`; commit there and push to origin.\n- Keep public entrypoint on existing callable objects (e.g., `CompiledFunction.Call`), no new public API entrypoint.\n[...]\n- User timeline: \"should land this week\".\n- No internet access (github.com unresolvable); origin likely the bare repo at `/srv/git/tengo.git`.\n\n[...]\n### Done\n- Explored repo: master at `3cad0da`; remote `origin/feature/callable-instance-isolation` exists with only scratch commits `9a50fcd`/`f8fdf1b` (additions to `scratch/callable-notes.md` only — not useful attempts).\n- Studied key code: `objects.go` (CompiledFunction, ObjectPtr, Copy, CanCall), `vm.go` (OpClosure/OpCall/OpReturn, frame handling, Run error wrapping), `compiler.go` (module compile/export), `script.go` (Compiled: Run/RunContext/Clone/Get/GetAll/Set), `tengo.go` (CallableFunc, ToInterface).\n[...]\n- **Return values from runFunction** pass through `resolveObject` so returned closures/composites stay callable.\n- New branch from master chosen over remote scratch branch (remote only had junk notes commits); pushing will likely need `--force` since remote name already exists.\n\n[...]\n4. `gofmt -w` on all changed files; `go vet` optionally.\n5. Commit on `feature/callable-instance-isolation`; push to origin (force push likely needed; remote currently at `f8fdf1b` with only scratch/callable-notes.md changes, local branch is master-based).\n6. Run `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` alone.\n[...]\n## Critical Context\n- Repo: `/app`, Go 1.25.5; module `github.com/d5/tengo/v2`; bare origin repo also at `/srv/git/tengo.git`; no network access.\n- master HEAD: `3cad0da`; remote feature branch: `f8fdf1b`/`9a50fcd` (scratch only).\n- Before fix: `c.Get(\"f\").Object().Call(...)` returned `(nil, nil)` despite `CanCall()==true`.\n- Key structures: `CompiledFunction{Instructions, NumLocals, NumParameters, VarArgs, SourceMap, Free []*ObjectPtr, ctx}`; `ObjectPtr{Value *Object}` (free vars); `Compiled{globalIndexes, bytecode, globals, maxAllocs, lock}`.\n- Error format reference: `\"Runtime Error: not callable: int\\n\\tat mod1:3:4\\n\\tat test:4:1\"`; arg-count: `\"wrong number of arguments: want>=2, got=0\"`.\n- Test helpers: `expectRun`/`expectError`/`expectErrorIs` (vm_test.go), `traceCompileRun` (checks non-empty stack), `compiledGet`/`compiledGetAll` (script_test.go); `require` package special-cases `*tengo.CompiledFunction` (compares formatted instructions, ignores Free/ctx).\n- `scripts` test scaffolding uses `example_test.go`; `cmd/bench` and `cmd/tengo` call `tengo.NewVM` directly (signature unchanged).\n[...]\n\n## Original Request\n- The visible user message in this session: \"No questions from my side yet. Keep going.\" (The original framing was in earlier, unseen context.)\n- The ongoing task (per the work performed): make Tengo compiled functions callable from Go code (`CompiledFunction.Call`) in the tengo repo at `/app`, with correct semantics for globals, imports, closure captures, variadic args, recursion, runtime error formatting, `Clone()` isolation, transfer of callables between `Compiled` instances (`Set`/`Script.Add`), and callbacks passed to Go `UserFunction`s.\n[...]\n- Core design established:\n  - `callCtx{code, globals, maxAllocs, globalNames, destNames, globalMap, runtime}`: callables keep their **origin bytecode** (constants/source maps) but resolve/mutate **destination globals** by name via `remapGlobals`/`globalMap`.\n  - VM frames carry per-frame `code`, `globalMap`, `layoutNames`; `VM` mirrors them (`ctx`, `globalMap`, `layoutNames`, `runtime`).\n[...]\n  - `Get`/`GetAll` return stored values with fallback binding; `Set` snapshots only foreign callables; `Clone` snapshots with shared capture cells preserved.\n- Bugs found/fixed: self-recursive closure infinite recursion; shared capture cells across globals; cross-script global index mismatch; missing globals → undefined; two VM hangs (compile-time ctx lacked global names → fixed by rebinding in `Script.Compile`; `Run()` reset used unset field → use `v.ctx`); zero-size `runtimeID` address aliasing (`_ byte` fix); frame `code` read after frame switch; double \"Runtime Error:\" prefix via Go callbacks; traversal rewrite accidentally dropped `Equals`/`SourcePos`/`CanCall` (re-added).\n- Temporary `OpConstant` binding experiment was added, caused a hang, debugged, then removed (perf/identity regression).\n- Scratch tests were consolidated into the permanent file `callable_test.go` (all pass).\n\n## Context Needed to Continue\n- Repo `/app` = `github.com/d5/tengo/v2`. Modified source files: `objects.go`, `script.go`, `vm.go`, `compiler.go`, `symbol_table.go`. Kept test file: `callable_test.go`. All other test files were scratch and deleted.\n- Validation pattern after each patch: `gofmt -w <files> && go build ./...` then `timeout 180 go test -count=1 ./...`; `go test -race -count=1 ./...` at milestones; use `timeout` wrappers because hangs occurred repeatedly.\n[...]\n\n1. **Deleted scratch tests** `repro_test.go`, `mod_test.go` — `rm -f`; checked via `go test ./...` (all ok). Done.\n2. **objects.go** — register `ObjectPtr` in `seen` before recursing (self-recursive closures); check: `gofmt -w`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`. Done.\n3. **script.go** — shared `seen` map across global roots in `Compile`/`Clone` so shared captures stay shared; same check run. Done.\n4. **objects.go + script.go + vm.go** — `callCtx` refactor to `code/globals/maxAllocs`; `Call` uses `ctx.code`; origin-code retention in `bindContext`; `Get`/`GetAll` no longer resolve at rest; check: `gofmt -w`, `go build ./...` → ok. Done.\n5. **objects.go** — full rewrite of traversal block (`sameRuntime`, `bindContext`, `containsCallable`, `boundTo`, `resolveObject`, `isolateObject`); build failed (missing `Equals`/`SourcePos`/`CanCall`) → re-added via python patch; check: `gofmt -w`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` → pass. Done.\n6. **objects.go + script.go + vm.go** — `globalNames`/`destNames`/`globalMap` + `remapGlobals`; `Compiled.globalNames` + `makeGlobalNames`; `newVM` global-names param; `mapGlobal`; Op{Get,Set,SetSel}Global remapping; build errors (`bytecode.globalNames`, missing VM fields) fixed; check: `gofmt -w`, `go build ./...`, tests. Done."}
{"id": "s017", "excerpt": "[...]\n- Transferred closures: destination sees captures as of transfer time; globals resolve against the destination instance; isolation must apply recursively to callables inside transferred arrays/maps; keep the public entrypoint on the current callable objects.\n- Work on new branch `feature/callable-instance-isolation` from master; commit and push to origin when done.\n\n[...]\n- (none)\n- Branch: `feature/callable-instance-isolation` created from master; must commit there and push to origin.\n- Final step must be `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` alone (no other command; cannot continue after).\n- Keep the public entrypoint on current callable objects (i.e., `CompiledFunction.Call`).\n- No internet (github.com unresolvable); origin must be reachable locally.\n- After two output-token-limit truncations, user system asked for concise replies ending with exactly one bash tool call.\n[...]\n- Explored codebase: `objects.go`, `vm.go`, `script.go`, `compiler.go`, `bytecode.go`, `tengo.go`, `errors.go`, `vm_test.go`, `script_test.go`, `require/require.go`.\n- Found `origin/feature/callable-instance-isolation` with only 2 placeholder commits (`9a50fcd`, `f8fdf1b` adding `scratch/callable-notes.md`); master HEAD = `3cad0da`. Bare mirror at `/srv/git/tengo.git` has same refs (no hidden implementation).\n- Created branch: `git checkout -b feature/callable-instance-isolation master` (clean tree).\n[...]\n- [ ] Edge cases not yet verified: clone isolation, cross-instance `Set` isolation, capture-snapshot-at-transfer semantics, error-string parity with in-script errors, variadic/recursion from Go, recursive isolation inside transferred arrays/maps.\n- [ ] Scratch test files `repro_test.go` / `mod_test.go` still in repo — remove or formalize into regression tests.\n- [ ] Not yet committed or pushed.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none) — build passes; no network but `origin` appears locally resolvable (push not yet verified; remote branch diverges due to placeholder commits).\n\n[...]\n3. Confirm runtime errors match expected strings in `vm_test.go` (`\"Runtime Error: ...\\n\\tat test:line:col\"`).\n4. Remove or convert scratch files `/app/repro_test.go`, `/app/mod_test.go`.\n5. Commit on `feature/callable-instance-isolation`; push to origin (remote branch has placeholder commits — check `git remote -v`, may need `--force-with-lease`).\n6. Finish with `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` alone.\n[...]\n## Critical Context\n- Repo `/app`; module `github.com/d5/tengo/v2`; go directive 1.13; toolchain go1.25.5. Refs: master=`3cad0da`; origin/feature/...=`f8fdf1b` (only touches `scratch/callable-notes.md`). Local branch from master diverges from remote → push likely needs force-with-lease. Bare repo: `/srv/git/tengo.git`.\n- Error formats: `\"Runtime Error: %w\\n\\tat %s\"` (via `formatError`); arg-count `\"wrong number of arguments: want=%d, got=%d\"` / variadic `\"want>=%d, got=%d\"`.\n[...]\n\n## Original Request\n\n[...]\n\n1. **callCtx redesign** (objects.go): holds `code` (origin bytecode for constants/source map), `globals` (destination storage), `maxAllocs`, `globalNames` (origin layout), `destNames` (destination layout), `globalMap` (index remapping), `runtime` (identity token).\n2. **Cycle-safe traversal**: replaced ad-hoc seen/funcs/containers param soup with `callableState{cells, funcs, containers}`; `bindContext`, `containsCallable`, `boundTo`, `resolveObject` (live/shared binding), `isolateObject` (snapshot isolation) are all cycle-safe and identity-preserving. `bindContext` returns early if `sameRuntime`.\n3. **Global remapping by name**: `remapGlobals(originNames, destNames)` maps origin global indexes to destination indexes; nil = identical layout; unmapped (`-1`) globals read as `undefined` and writes are dropped. VM `mapGlobal()` used in `OpGetGlobal`/`OpSetGlobal`/`OpSetSelGlobal`, hardened with bounds checks.\n4. **Per-frame execution context** (vm.go `frame` gains `code`, `globalMap`, `layoutNames`): transferred callables carry their own bytecode/constants/file set; frame push/pop switches `v.constants`, `v.fileSet`, `v.globalMap`, `v.layoutNames`; `formatError` uses per-frame file sets; `OpClosure` builds closure ctx from executing frame layout.\n5. **Block-scoped global names** (symbol_table.go): root symbol table now tracks `globalNames`/`maxGlobal`; `SymbolTable.GlobalNames()` feeds `Compiled.globalNames` so block-scoped globals remap correctly across instances.\n[...]\n9. **Error formats**: `Call()` errors match runtime format; nested VM errors crossing Go callbacks have the duplicate `Runtime Error: ` prefix stripped; known/accepted diff: in-script `Run()` error includes an extra caller frame line vs Go `Call()` (verified in a test and documented as expected).\n10. **Bugs found via tests**: frame-switch ordering (read `curFrame.code` before switching), `Run()` resetting `layoutNames` from unset VM field (hang), missing global-names at compile time (hang), zero-sized runtimeID, missing `Equals`/`SourcePos`/`CanCall` after rewrite (empty `Equals` returns false, matching original semantics).\n\n[...]\n- Repo is `/app`, package `github.com/d5/tengo/v2`. All edits were applied via python3 heredoc patch scripts + `gofmt -w` + `go build ./...` + test runs.\n- Key invariants: origin code/constants preserved on transfer; globals resolve against destination instance; captures snapshot at transfer time but stay shared within one isolation pass (shared `callableState`); recursion works through `state.funcs`/`callableState.funcs`.\n- New internal APIs: `newVM(bytecode, globals, maxAllocs, globalNames, runtime)`, `callCtx` fields above, `runtimeID{_ byte}`, `symbolTable.GlobalNames()`, `bindCodeContext`, `mapGlobal` returning `-1` when unmapped, `isolateObject`/`resolveObject`/`boundTo`/`containsCallable` taking `*callableState`.\n- Regression tests live in untracked `/app/callable_test.go` (mustRun helper + TestCompiledFunction_* / TestCompiled_* / TestScript_* covering: Go calls w/ globals/variadics/recursion/state sharing, error formats, module exports, clone isolation, Set transfer isolation, callback args + isolation, recursive local closures, TCO via Go call, Script.Add callable isolation, RunContext).\n- Scratch tests were created and removed (`verify_test.go`→`edge_test.go`→...→ consolidated); final `git status` earlier showed M compiler.go, M objects.go, M script.go, M vm.go (+ symbol_table.go modified later) and untracked callable_test.go.\n\n[...]\n| 2 | script.go | Compile/Clone: single shared `seen` map across globals (shared captures stay shared) | same run as #1 | Done |\n| 3 | objects.go | callCtx split `code`/`globals`; Call uses `ctx.code`; bindContext keeps origin code | gofmt, go build | Done |\n| 4 | vm.go | rename `bytecode`→`code` in ctx construction | go build | Done |\n| 5 | script.go | callCtx literal update | go build | Done |\n| 6 | objects.go | rewrite traversal helpers (cycle-safe, identity-preserving, containers maps); accidentally dropped Equals/SourcePos/CanCall then re-added | go build, go test ./... (all pass) | Done |\n| 7 | compiler.go | (read-only) checked literal compilation for constant-pool question | grep | Done |\n| 8 | verify_test.go (scratch) | comprehensive scenario tests; iterated fixes (script syntax, source positions, holder declared via `Add` before `Compile`) | `go test -run TestVerify -v .` | Replaced |\n| 9 | objects.go | `remapGlobals` + `globalNames`/`globalMap` fields; unmapped globals → undefined | go build, tests | Done |\n[...]\n| 12 | vm.go | per-frame `code`/`globalMap`, constants/fileSet switching, `frameFileSet`, OpClosure ctx | go test (fixed frame-switch ordering bug) | Done |\n| 13 | transfer2_test.go (scratch) | in-script call of transferred callable; expectation fixed to 1020 (shared capture) | `go test -run TestTransferInScriptCall -v .` | Passed, removed |\n| 14 | objects.go | `funcs` map / then `callableState` refactor (cells/funcs/containers) | go build, go test | Done |\n| 15 | edge_test.go (scratch) | recursive local closures, clone shared captures, composite returns, transferred global fn, callback transfer isolation | `go test -run TestEdge -v .` (fixed Go compile errors via sed/python) | Passed, removed |\n| 16 | block_test.go, blk_test.go (scratch) | block-scoped global transfer by name; missing-name → undefined | `go test -run TestBlock -v .` | Passed, removed |\n| 17 | objects.go, script.go, vm.go | `destNames` field + big traversal rewrite; ctx wiring | go build, full + race tests pass | Done |\n| 18 | compiler.go | `Bytecode()` binds code contexts (`bindCodeContext`) — caused hang | timeout tests exposed hang; instrumented VM panic (temporary) | Fixed |\n[...]\n| 29 | callable_test.go (final) | consolidated all regression tests (rm verify/edge/cb/blk/more/errfmt) | `go test -count=1 -run 'TestCompiledFunction|TestCompiled_' -v .` | Retained |\n| 30 | vm.go | strip nested `Runtime Error: ` prefix across Go callback boundary (added errors/strings imports) | cberr_test.go (scratch) `go test -run TestCallbackErrorFormat` | Done |\n| 31 | objects.go | `bindContext` early return on `sameRuntime` (drop !snapshot guard) | rec_test.go (scratch, transferred recursive closure) | Passed, removed |\n| 32 | vm.go | nested constant-fn calls inherit caller's globalMap when bytecode matches | full suite | Done |\n| 33 | compiler.go | `bindCodeContextSeen`: cycle-safe, skip live runtimes | full suite | Done |\n| 34 | tco_test.go (scratch) | TCO via Go call (sum 5000→12502500), Script.Add callable (115), RunContext (4) | targeted `-run` tests after fixing test bugs | Merged into #29, removed |\n| 35 | callable_test.go | appended TCO / Add-isolation / RunContext tests; added `context` import | `go test -run 'TestCompiledFunction|TestCompiled_|TestScript_' -v .` | Done |"}
